+// Venture: a count can change between a vkEnumerate* count call and its fill call (a hybrid
+// laptop's loader adding or dropping a GPU, a driver answering differently between calls). The
+// fill then returns VK_INCOMPLETE, which is not an error: the array holds valid entries.
+// Repeat count+fill a bounded number of times while it is incomplete, then accept the entries
+// the last fill returned.
+constexpr int kEnumerateAttemptsVENTURE = 4;
+template <typename T, typename Enumerate>
+VkResult EnumerateAllVENTURE(std::vector<T> *out, Enumerate &&enumerate, const T &blank = T{})
+{
+    for (int attempt = 0; attempt < kEnumerateAttemptsVENTURE; ++attempt)
+    {
+        uint32_t count  = 0;
+        VkResult result = enumerate(&count, static_cast<T *>(nullptr));
+        if (result < VK_SUCCESS)
+        {
+            out->clear();
+            return result;
+        }
+        out->assign(count, blank);
+        if (count == 0)
+        {
+            return VK_SUCCESS;
+        }
+        result = enumerate(&count, out->data());
+        if (result < VK_SUCCESS)
+        {
+            out->clear();
+            return result;
+        }
+        if (count < out->size())
+        {
+            out->resize(count);
+        }
+        if (result != VK_INCOMPLETE)
+        {
+            return VK_SUCCESS;
+        }
+    }
+    return VK_SUCCESS;
+}
